>First off, no I don't mind spoilers at all.

Good.

  Etch this in your brain:  "Travel fast, type slow."  The faster you
travel, the less chance of a summoning storm that will snowball into an
unwinnable situation.  The more time you spending fighting, the more
chance there is of a situation snowballing out of control.

  The faster you type, the less thinking you're doing.  The Endgame
especially involves major context switches as you portal from one plane
to the next.

  The most important item to have with you when you exit Dlvl 1 is the
Amulet of Yendor.  I'm not kidding.  Players have left the Dungeons of
Doom without the AoY.

  The second most important item is an Ascension state of mind.
Determine that you will stop and think at every point and do what's
necessary to continue.  If you don't, you won't Ascend.

  The third thing is every charged wand of teleport you've found so far.
Every last one of them.  Even be burdened if necessary.  Wands of
teleport can make up for that, and you can drop them as you use them up.
So being burdened with /oTele is a self-correcting problem.

  I watched a player get mobbed five deep in the center the Plane of Air
on NAO.  They ran out of mana, and read a non-blessed scroll of genocide
while confused.  Even the "oLS they were wearing didn't save them from
expiring due to genocidal confusion.  A few /oTele could probably have
prevented that.

  There are a lot of things tied for fourth place, but you seem to have
most of them.  You want at least two non-cursed scrolls of gold
detection to read while confused on the Planes of Fire and Water.
You will also need two ?oGD for the Planes of Earth and Air.

  You will *want* three or four more c?oGD to help zero in on the moving
portal on the Plane of Water.  I do this a lot and it's a great help.

  On Fire do the confused read of the ?oGD asap.  On water, wait until
you've traveled to the middle of the Plane first.

  On earth and air you can do confused read of ?oGD, or just read a
c?oGD, which is faster.  If you do the cursed ?oGD REMEMBER WHERE THE
PORTAL IS.  (Or stick your mouse pointer over it.)  The '$' symbol
marking the portal that results from reading a c?oGD will disappear when
it gets into your line of sight.


  Save a b?oGenocide for when you enter the Plane of Water.  Then
blessed genocide ';'.  That way there won't be replacement monsters
generated when you enter the level.  Some players think this is
unnecessary.  This is probably not the time to check if they're wrong.

  You can levitate safely over the water on the Plane of Water.  NB:
Water Walking boots do NOT work on the Plane of Water.  (No, that
doesn't seem to make sense.  Don't ask me.  It wasn't my decision.)


