  Yes.  It's called the Ascension Run for a reason: You should be
running like a coward.  Don't fight unless you have NO other choice.
That means carry *every* wand of teleport you've found so far to
teleport monsters out of your way, if necessary.

  When is it necessary to teleport monsters out of your way?  Only when
you're *completely* blocked and you cannot move yourself out of the way.
Teleportitis, scrolls of teleportation, c!oGL, and teleport control are
your friends until you leave the Dungeons of Doom.  So use them in the
dungeon so you can save /oTele charges for the Planes.

  Save a few wands of Tele with a single charge for breaking when you
get mobbed on the Elemental/Astral Planes.  Breaking a charged /oTele
will teleport away every monster around you.  

  Yes, 11 out of 12 times a teleported Rider will end up next to you.
So what?  If they aren't next to you already breaking a /oTele won't
teleport them.  And they may end up in a position where they're not
blocking you any more.



