  Increasing your XL will make the spell of magic missile more
effective.  At XL 24 it will do [(XL/2) +1]d6 = 13d6.  That's an average
of 45.5 points of damage per hit, per monster, at range.  Makes even
Grayswandir's max of 38 points of damage, with max one hit, on one
monster, at melee distance look sick.

  Since your Int is greater than 18 you'll get another two points of
damage added to that: Average 47.5.

  Get up to XL 30 and you'll do ([(30/2) +1]d6) + 2 = 16d6 +2 = average
58 points of damage per hit per monster.

  That's a pretty big hammer.  Just remember to save mana for it for
when it's absolutely necessary.  (And it won't work against monsters
with MR or reflection.)  And, *IF* you can do so safely, drop the Amulet
of Yendor before casting it, to save the extra mana drain that comes
from spell casting while carrying the AoY.  Do NOT forget to pick it
back up.

